  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2 to exercise the max_mixed bound of workflows §6.4. Nine state facts, each read by an authored complementary pair of permissions (deskMember_i = true / deskMember_i ≠ true): an eq and a neq literal on the same binding and right operand, so one variable with opposite polarities, and both occurrences in permissions — one raises the verdict, the other lowers it, so each unknown flag is mixed. Nine unknown flags is k = 9 > max_mixed (8): the fallback completes them independently and records verdict.exact = false. Scenario 2 sits at the bound (k = 8) and is the case where exactness decides: flag 1 is known true, so pair 1 offers only its member route, pending on the manager's approval; the other eight pairs give a ready route for every value of their flags, but completed independently they could all fail, leaving Pending. Built after decisions/0003, which made duty guards uniform and so retired the nine-guard case (now due2-conditional-duties) as a test of the bound.",
